  "description": "“A durable but lightweight aluminum frame, easy-to-use sliding dropouts, and capable all-rounder geometry… a gravel bike worth mythologizing.” - from Bikepacking.com's long term review of Chessie.\n\nMeet Chessie, our monstrous new aluminum alloy frameset, named after the legendary sea creature said to lurk in the Chesapeake Bay. But unlike its mythical namesake, this beast is very real—and it’s ready to tackle the wildest gravel and bikepacking routes you can throw at it.\nForget what you thought you knew about aluminum. Advances in tubing and design have transformed it from the jarring rides of old into something truly refined. Chessie’s double-butted main triangle and meticulously selected tubing deliver an exhilarating, smooth ride with all the stiffness you need to charge ahead. It's custom, sliding dropouts allow for easy single-speed setups while using flat-mount brakes and still giving you room for fenders.\nThe triple-butted fork is a true performer, ready for racks, fenders, and cargo cages. Its elegant segmented design complements the frame without looking overbuilt, and the frame clearance is as generous as Chessie’s appetite: up to 700x50mm or 650x2.25” tires on Medium and larger sizes and 650bx2.1” or 26x2.25” on Small and XS sizes. If you're keen on running fenders, you can mount 700x45 or 650bx45, respectively.\nThis frameset has already proven its chops—Nic piloted one through the Mega Mid South, a brutal 300-mile self-supported ride with 17,000 feet of climbing. Whether you’re racing, adventuring, or just getting lost on purpose, Chessie is here to make every ride legendary.\nAre you ready to wake the monster? Find build ideas here!\nIf you want to dig into more of the nitty gritty, check out our Monster Guide (pdf download).\n\nTire Clearance w/o Fenders: Up to 700x50 or 650bx2.25\" (M, L, and XL sizes) / 650bx2.1\" or 26x2.25\" (S and XS) sizes.\n\nTire Clearance w Fenders: 700x45 (M, L, and XL sizes) or 650bx45 (S and XS sizes).\n\nBB: English threaded 68mm. Uses Gravel Chain line of 47 mm or greater.\n\nBrakes: Flat mount, 160mm rotors minimum. Front uses 160mm without needing any adaptors.\n\nSeatpost: 27.2 (seat collar included). Compatible with internal dropper posts.\n\nFrame Eyelets: Eyelets on rear dropouts for racks and fenders.\n\nFork Eyelets: Eyelets on fork dropouts. Triple thru-bosses on the blades for cargo/water bottle cages.\n\nCable Routing: External on the downtube and internal dropper routing on the seat tube.\n\nPaint: Shoreline Sand or Leviathan Blue with Velo Orange decal and metal headbadge\n\nPlease note: the blue frame does not have the rack mounts on the monostay. It is being discontinued once it is out of stock.\nGeometry",
